        "full_raw_final_answer_text": "To find the percentage decrease of the surface area, we first calculate the surface area of the original block and then determine the change caused by the cut-out section.\n\n1.  **Original Surface Area**:\n    The original block has dimensions:\n    *   Length ($L$) = 12\n    *   Width ($W$) = 6\n    *   Height ($H$) = 8\n    \n    The surface area is:\n    $$A_{\\text{original}} = 2(LW + LH + WH) = 2(12 \\times 6 + 12 \\times 8 + 6 \\times 8) = 2(72 + 96 + 48) = 2(216) = 432$$\n\n2.  **Surface Area Change**:\n    The cut-out section removes material from the corner. Based on the labels:\n    *   The section has a depth of 3 (label \"3\" on the right).\n    *   The height of the cut face on the left is 5 (label \"5\").\n    *   The shape of the vertical cut-out is a trapezoid with parallel vertical sides of height 8 (front left edge) and height $8 - 5 = 3$ (inner edge). The width of this face is the depth of the block, 6.\n\n    **Area Lost**:\n    *   Top face removed: $3 \\text{ (width)} \\times 6 \\text{ (depth)} = 18$.\n    *   Front face removed: A trapezoid with area $\\frac{8 + 3}{2} \\times 3 = \\frac{11}{2} \\times 3 = 16.5$.\n    *   Left face removed: A trapezoid with area $\\frac{8 + 3}{2} \\times 3 = 16.5$.\n    *   Total Area Lost = $18 + 16.5 + 16.5 = 51$.\n\n    **Area Gained**:\n    *   New horizontal face (bottom of the cut): $3 \\text{ (width)} \\times 6 \\text{ (depth)} = 18$.\n    *   New inner vertical face (right wall of the cut): This face has the same dimensions as the removed left face (width 6, heights 8 and 3). Area = $16.5$.\n    *   New vertical face (back of the cut): This face has the same dimensions as the removed front face (depth 6, heights 8 and 3). Area = $16.5$.\n    *   Total Area Gained = $18 + 16.5 + 16.5 = 51$.\n\n3.  **Conclusion**:\n    Since the total area lost ($51$) is exactly equal to the total area gained ($51$), the net change in surface area is 0. Therefore, the decrease percentage is $0\\%$.\n\nSince $0\\%$ is less than $12.5\\%$, the correct choice is A.\n\nA",
